 logits.transpose(-1, -2).mul(a_m)).view(BHL, L).softmax(dim=-1).view(B, H, L, L))\nprofile_section(\\\"lerp p_mix\\\", lambda: torch.lerp(p0, p1, beta))\nprofile_section(\\\"G = x@x.T\\\", lambda: x @ x.transpose(-1, -2))\nprofile_section(\\\"p1 @ G\\\", lambda: p1 @ G_exp)\nprofile_section(\\\"p_mix @ G\\\", lambda: p_mix @ G_exp)\nprofile_section(\\\"p_mix @ v\\\", lambda: p_mix @ v)\nprofile_section(\\\"norm computation\\\", lambda: (p1 @ G_exp).mul(p1).sum(dim=-1, keepdim=True).sqrt_().clamp_min_(1e-6))\n\n# Test the stacked Gram approach\nprint(\\\"\\\\n--- Stacked Gram optimization test ---\\\")\ndef stacked_gram(p1, p_mix, G):\n    B, H, L, _ = p1.shape\n    p_stack = torch.cat([p1.reshape(B, H*L, L), p_mix.reshape(B, H*L, L)], dim=1)\n    result = p_stack @ G  # (B, 2*H*L, L)\n    p1G = result[:, :H*L, :].reshape(B, H, L, L)\n    pmG = result[:, H*L:, :].reshape(B, H, L, L)\n    return p1G, pmG\n\n# Verify correctness\np1G_orig = p1 @ G_exp\npmG_orig = p_mix @ G_exp\np1G_new, pmG_new = stacked_gram(p1, p_mix, G)\nprint(f\\\"p1G max diff: {torch.max(torch.abs(p1G_orig - p1G_new)):.2e}\\\")\nprint(f\\\"pmG max diff: {torch.max(torch.abs(pmG_orig - pmG_new)):.2e}\\\")\n\nprofile_section(\\\"2 separate p@G (broadcast)\\\", lambda: (p1 @ G_exp, p_mix @ G_exp))\nprofile_section(\\\"stacked p@G (bmm)\\\", lambda: stacked_gram(p1, p_mix, G))\n\nEOF\npython3 /tmp/profile_test.py\"","aggregated_output":"Full function median: 50.06 ms\n\nBreakdown:\n  q projection: 6.44 ms\n  k projection: 6.40 ms\n  v projection: 6.48 ms\n  q@k.T logits: 1.33 ms\n  softmax p0: 5.58 ms\n  p1_logits + softmax: 7.59 ms\n  lerp p_mix: 0.16 ms\n  G = x@x.T: 1.52 ms\n  p1 @ G: 5.80 ms\n  p_mix @ G: 5.62 ms\n  p_mix @ v: 1.28 ms\n  norm computation: 6.12 ms\n\n--- Stacked Gram optimization test ---\np1G max diff: 0.00e+00\npmG max diff: 0.00e+00\n  2 separate p@G (broadcast): 11.72 ms\n  stacked p@G (bmm): 10.82 ms\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"agent_message","text":"Good, profiling data is clear. The stacked Gram gives a small win (~8%). Softmax is surprisingly expensive. Let me explore more optimizations.\n\nKey observations:\n- 3 projections: ~19ms total (38% of total)\n- 2 softmaxes: ~13ms (26% of total)\n- 2 p@G: ~11ms (22% of total)\n- G + logits + p@v + lerp + norm + output: ~7ms (14%)\n\nThe stacked Gram gives ~1ms savings. Let me think about bigger wins.\n\n**Softmax optimization**: The softmax is on (BHL, L) = 5120 × 256 for the largest case. That's a lot of rows. Can we speed this up?\n\nActually, wait. Let me also check: what if we use direct 4D softmax instead of view+2D+view?\n\nAlso, let me think about whether we can avoid computing p0 explicitly. p_mix = (1-beta)*p0 + beta*p1. We need p_mix for output and norms. We also need p1 for norm1. But do we need p0 for anything besides p_mix? \n\nLooking at the code: p0 is only used in `torch.lerp(p0, p1, beta)`. So yes, we need it.\n\nBut wait - what if we compute p_mix differently? Since p_mix is a linear combination of two softmaxes, there's no mathematical simplification. We need both p0 and p1.\n\nLet me look at bigger wins. What about fusing the projections? \n\nCurrently we do 3 separate (B*L, C) @ (C, H*D) matmuls. What if we concatenate wq, wk, wv into a single (3*H*D, C) matrix and do one big matmul? Then split afterwards.\n\nThis would replace 3 matmuls of size (B*L, C) @ (C, H*D) with one matmul of size (B*L, C) @ (C, 3*H*D). Same total FLOPs but one larger matmul → better cache efficiency.\n\nLet me test this.\n\nAlso, let me think about the output computation. Currently we return `y.transpose(1, 2).flatten(2).contiguous()` where y is (B, H, L, D). This creates the (B, L, H*D) output. Can we avoid the contiguous copy at the end? Probably not, since the output needs to be a certain layout.\n\nWait, actually. What if we compute v in (B, L, H, D) layout, compute attention output in (B, L, H, D) layout, and just flatten? But attention requires q and k in (B, H, L, D) for per-head attention. We'd need to transpose anyway.\n\nLet me try the fused projection idea and also check a few more things.\nProfile shows projections (~19ms), softmaxes (~13ms), and Gram multiplies (~11ms) are the main costs. Let me test the fused 3-in-1 projection and other optimizations."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"cat > /tmp/profile_test2.py << 'EOF'\nimport time, math\nimport torch\n\ntorch.set_num_threads(1)\ntorch.set_num_interop_threads(1)\n\nB, L, C, H, D = 1, 256, 1280, 20, 64\n\ntorch.manual_seed(42)\nx = torch.randn(B, L, C)\nwq = torch.randn(H, D, C)\nwk = torch.randn(H, D, C)\nwv = torch.randn(H, D, C)\nalpha = 1.05\nbeta = 7.5\n\ndef profile(name, fn, warmup=3, repeats=11):\n    for _ in range(warmup):\n        fn()\n    times = []\n    for _ in range(repeats):\n        t0 = time.process_time_ns()\n        fn()\n        times.append((time.process_time_ns() - t0) / 1e6)\n    print(f\\\"  {name}: {sorted(times)[5]:.2f} ms\\\")\n\nxr = x.reshape(B * L, C)\nHD = H * D\n\n# Current: 3 separate projections\ndef three_proj():\n    q = (xr @ wq.reshape(HD, C).T).reshape(B, L, H, D).permute(0, 2, 1, 3).contiguous()\n    k = (xr @ wk.reshape(HD, C).T).reshape(B, L, H, D).permute(0, 2, 1, 3).contiguous()\n    v = (xr @ wv.reshape(HD, C).T).reshape(B, L, H, D).permute(0, 2, 1, 3).contiguous()\n    return q, k, v\n\n# Fused: 1 big projection then split\ndef fused_proj():\n    w_all = torch.cat([wq.reshape(HD, C), wk.reshape(HD, C), wv.reshape(HD, C)], dim=0)  # (3*HD, C)\n    out = xr @ w_all.T  # (B*L, 3*HD)\n    q, k, v = out.split([HD, HD, HD], dim=1)\n    q = q.reshape(B, L, H, D).permute(0, 2, 1, 3).contiguous()\n    k = k.reshape(B, L, H, D).permute(0, 2, 1, 3).contiguous()\n    v = v.reshape(B, L, H, D).permute(0, 2, 1, 3).contiguous()\n    return q, k, v\n\nprint(\\\"Projection options:\\\")\nprofile(\\\"3 separate projs\\\", three_proj)\nprofile(\\\"fused proj + split\\\", fused_proj)\n\n# Verify\nq1, k1, v1 = three_proj()\nq2, k2, v2 = fused_proj()\nprint(f\\\"  q diff: {torch.max(torch.abs(q1 - q2)):.2e}\\\")\nprint(f\\\"  k diff: {torch.max(torch.abs(k1 - k2)):.2e}\\\")\nprint(f\\\"  v diff: {torch.max(torch.abs(v1 - v2)):.2e}\\\")\n\n# Softmax: 4D vs view+2D+view\nq, k, v = three_proj()\ninv_sqrt_d = 1.0 / math.sqrt(D)\nlogits = q @ k.transpose(-1, -2)\nlogits.mul_(inv_sqrt_d)\nBHL = B * H * L\n\nprint(\\\"\\\\nSoftmax options:\\\")\nprofile(\\\"view(BHL,L)+softmax+view\\\", lambda: logits.view(BHL, L).softmax(dim=-1).view(B, H, L, L))\nprofile(\\\"direct 4D softmax dim=-1\\\", lambda: logits.softmax(dim=-1))\nprofile(\\\"direct 4D softmax dim=3\\\", lambda: torch.softmax(logits, dim=3))\n\n# Verify\ns1 = logits.view(BHL, L).softmax(dim=-1).view(B, H, L, L)\ns2 = logits.softmax(dim=-1)\nprint(f\\\"  diff: {torch.max(torch.abs(s1 - s2)):.2e}\\\")\n\n# Can we combine the p1 logits computation more efficiently?\na_p = 0.5 * (1.0 + alpha)\na_m = 0.5 * (1.0 - alpha)\n\nprint(\\\"\\\\np1 logits options:\\\")\nprofile(\\\"mul + add (current)\\\", lambda: logits.mul(a_p).add_(logits.transpose(-1, -2), alpha=a_m))\nprofile(\\\"lerp-style: a_p*A + a_m*A\"'^T\", lambda: a_p * logits + a_m * logits.transpose(-1, -2))\n# Using addcmul? \nprofile(\"addcmul style\", lambda: logits.transpose(-1, -2).mul(a_m).add_(logits, alpha=a_p))\n\n# Test 4D softmax vs 2D view softmax for the p1 case too\np1_logits = logits.mul(a_p)\np1_logits.add_(logits.transpose(-1, -2), alpha=a_m)\n\nprint(\"'\"\\\\np1 softmax:\\\")\nprofile(\\\"view+2D+view\\\", lambda: p1_logits.view(BHL, L).softmax(dim=-1).view(B, H, L, L))\nprofile(\\\"direct 4D\\\", lambda: p1_logits.softmax(dim=-1))\n\n# Now test if we can compute the norm without p_mix @ G separately\n# Idea: since p_mix = (1-b)*p0 + b*p1\n# ||p_mix @ x||\"'^2 = (p_mix @ G) * p_mix sum_last = sum of elements\n# = (1-b)''^2 * (p0@G * p0).sum + b''^2 * (p1@G * p1).sum + 2*(1-b)*b * (p0@G * p1).sum\n# This means we need p0@G too. Same total cost.\n\n# But what if we stack all three: p0, p1, p_mix? No, p_mix is the combination.\n\n# Let'\"'s try another idea: compute norms via p@x directly but only for 1 head?\n# No, we need per-head norms.\n\n# What about computing p0@G and p1@G in one stacked matmul, then deriving normm?\n# We'd still need the same total FLOPs for p@G.\n\n# Wait - let me check: is the in-place mul_ on the result of p@G free?\np1 = p1_logits.view(BHL, L).softmax(dim=-1).view(B, H, L, L)\np0 = logits.view(BHL, L).softmax(dim=-1).view(B, H, L, L)\np_mix = torch.lerp(p0, p1, beta)\nG = x @ x.transpose(-1, -2)\nG_exp = G.unsqueeze(1)\n\nprint(\\\"\\\\nNorm computation options:\\\")\nprofile(\\\"p@G + mul_ + sum + sqrt + clamp\\\", lambda: (p1 @ G_exp).mul_(p1).sum(dim=-1, keepdim=True).sqrt_().clamp_min_(1e-6))\nprofile(\\\"p@G (just matmul)\\\", lambda: p1 @ G_exp)\nprofile(\\\"mul + sum\\\", lambda: p1G.mul(p1).sum(dim=-1, keepdim=True))\n\np1G = p1 @ G_exp\nprofile(\\\"p1G.clone().mul_(p1)\\\", lambda: p1G.clone().mul_(p1))\n\n# What about torch.einsum for the norm? norm_sq = einsum(\\\"bhli,bhlj,bij->bhl\\\", p, p, G)\n# That's BHL\"'^2 * L = BHL''^3 same as p@G then dot.\n\n# Actually wait: (p @ G) * p summed over last = sum_j (p @ G)[j] * p[j] = sum_j sum_k p_k G_kj p_j = p''^T G p \n# This is a quadratic form. Can we compute it more efficiently?\n# In batched form: for each row p_i of p (size L), compute p_i @ G @ p_i''^T\n# Total: BHL * (L''^2 + L) ≈ BHL''^3, same as before.\n\n# Let me try: compute each row'\"'s quadratic form directly\nprint(\\\"\\\\nQuadratic form options:\\\")\n# Method 1: p@G then elementwise multiply and sum (current)\ndef norm_via_matmul(p, G):\n    G_exp = G.unsqueeze(1)\n    pG = p @ G_exp\n    return pG.mul(p).sum(dim=-1, keepdim=True)\n\n# Method 2: einsum\ndef norm_via_einsum(p, G):\n    # p: (B,H,L,L), G: (B,L,L)\n    # result[i,j,k] = sum_l sum_m p[i,j,k,l] * G[i,l,m] * p[i,j,k,m]\n    # = sum_l p[i,j,k,l] * (G @ p[i,j,k,:].T)[l]\n    return torch.einsum(\\\"bhli,bij,bhlj->bhl\\\", p, G, p).unsqueeze(-1)\n\nprofile(\\\"p@G + mul + sum\\\", lambda: norm_via_matmul(p1, G))\nprofile(\\\"einsum quadratic\\\", lambda: norm_via_einsum(p1, G))\n\nn1 = norm_via_matmul(p1, G)\nn2 = norm_via_einsum(p1, G)\nprint(f\\\"  diff: {torch.max(torch.abs(n1 - n2)):.2e}\\\")\n\n# Another idea: can we compute both norms (norm1 and normm) more efficiently?\n# Since p_mix = (1-b)*p0 + b*p1:\n# normm\"'^2 = (1-b)''^2 * norm0''^2 + b''^2 * norm1''^2 + 2*b*(1-b) * cross\n# where cross = (p0 @ G) * p1 sum over last\n# This requires p0@G instead of p_mix@G. Same cost.\n# But we could stack p0 and p1 for one big matmul.\n\nprint(\"'\"\\\\nStacked p0+p1 @ G:\\\")\ndef stacked_p0_p1_G(p0, p1, G):\n    B, H, L, _ = p0.shape\n    ps = torch.cat([p0.reshape(B, H*L, L), p1.reshape(B, H*L, L)], dim=1)  # (B, 2HL, L)\n    result = ps @ G  # (B, 2HL, L)\n    p0G = result[:, :H*L, :].reshape(B, H, L, L)\n    p1G = result[:, H*L:, :].reshape(B, H, L, L)\n    return p0G, p1G\n\nprofile(\\\"stacked p0+p1 @ G\\\", lambda: stacked_p0_p1_G(p0, p1, G))\nprofile(\\\"2 separate @G (broadcast)\\\", lambda: (p0 @ G_exp, p1 @ G_exp))\n\np0G_s, p1G_s = stacked_p0_p1_G(p0, p1, G)\np0G_d = p0 @ G_exp\np1G_d = p1 @ G_exp\nprint(f\\\"  p0G diff: {torch.max(torch.abs(p0G_s - p0G_d)):.2e}\\\")\nprint(f\\\"  p1G diff: {torch.max(torch.abs(p1G_s - p1G_d)):.2e}\\\")\n\n# Now compute normm from p0G and p1G\ndef normm_from_p0_p1(p0G, p1G, p0, p1, beta):\n    # p_mix = (1-b)*p0 + b*p1\n    # normm\"'^2 = sum over last dim of: p_mix @ G * p_mix\n    # = sum of: ((1-b)*p0G + b*p1G) * ((1-b)*p0 + b*p1)\n    b0 = 1.0 - beta\n    pmG = p0G.mul(b0).add_(p1G, alpha=beta)\n    pm = p0.mul(b0).add_(p1, alpha=beta)\n    return pmG.mul(pm).sum(dim=-1, keepdim=True)\n\n# Check vs direct\npmG = p_mix @ G_exp\nnormm_direct = pmG.mul(p_mix).sum(dim=-1, keepdim=True)\nnormm_cross = normm_from_p0_p1(p0G_d, p1G_d, p0, p1, beta)\nprint(f\"  normm diff: {torch.max(torch.abs(normm_direct - normm_cross)):.2e}\")\n\nEOF\npython3 /tmp/profile_test2.py'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"cat > /tmp/profile_test2.py << 'EOF'\nimport time, math\nimport torch\n\ntorch.set_num_threads(1)\ntorch.set_num_interop_threads(1)\n\nB, L, C, H, D = 1, 256, 1280, 20, 64\n\ntorch.manual_seed(42)\nx = torch.randn(B, L, C)\nwq = torch.randn(H, D, C)\nwk = torch.randn(H, D, C)\nwv = torch.randn(H, D, C)\nalpha = 1.05\nbeta = 7.5\n\ndef profile(name, fn, warmup=3, repeats=11):\n    for _ in range(warmup):\n        fn()\n    times = []\n    for _ in range(repeats):\n        t0 = time.process_time_ns()\n        fn()\n        times.append((time.process_time_ns() - t0) / 1e6)\n    print(f\\\"  {name}: {sorted(times)[5]:.2f} ms\\\")\n\nxr = x.reshape(B * L, C)\nHD = H * D\n\n# Current: 3 separate projections\ndef three_proj():\n    q = (xr @ wq.reshape(HD, C).T).reshape(B, L, H, D).permute(0, 2, 1, 3).contiguous()\n    k = (xr @ wk.reshape(HD, C).T).reshape(B, L, H, D).permute(0, 2, 1, 3).contiguous()\n    v = (xr @ wv.reshape(HD, C).T).reshape(B, L, H, D).permute(0, 2, 1, 3).contiguous()\n    return q, k, v\n\n# Fused: 1 big projection then split\ndef fused_proj():\n    w_all = torch.cat([wq.reshape(HD, C), wk.reshape(HD, C), wv.reshape(HD, C)], dim=0)  # (3*HD, C)\n    out = xr @ w_all.T  # (B*L, 3*HD)\n    q, k, v = out.split([HD, HD, HD], dim=1)\n    q = q.reshape(B, L, H, D).permute(0, 2, 1, 3).contiguous()\n    k = k.reshape(B, L, H, D).permute(0, 2, 1, 3).contiguous()\n    v = v.reshape(B, L, H, D).permute(0, 2, 1, 3).contiguous()\n    return q, k, v\n\nprint(\\\"Projection options:\\\")\nprofile(\\\"3 separate projs\\\", three_proj)\nprofile(\\\"fused proj + split\\\", fused_proj)\n\n# Verify\nq1, k1, v1 = three_proj()\nq2, k2, v2 = fused_proj()\nprint(f\\\"  q diff: {torch.max(torch.abs(q1 - q2)):.2e}\\\")\nprint(f\\\"  k diff: {torch.max(torch.abs(k1 - k2)):.2e}\\\")\nprint(f\\\"  v diff: {torch.max(torch.abs(v1 - v2)):.2e}\\\")\n\n# Softmax: 4D vs view+2D+view\nq, k, v = three_proj()\ninv_sqrt_d = 1.0 / math.sqrt(D)\nlogits = q @ k.transpose(-1, -2)\nlogits.mul_(inv_sqrt_d)\nBHL = B * H * L\n\nprint(\\\"\\\\nSoftmax options:\\\")\nprofile(\\\"view(BHL,L)+softmax+view\\\", lambda: logits.view(BHL, L).softmax(dim=-1).view(B, H, L, L))\nprofile(\\\"direct 4D softmax dim=-1\\\", lambda: logits.softmax(dim=-1))\nprofile(\\\"direct 4D softmax dim=3\\\", lambda: torch.softmax(logits, dim=3))\n\n# Verify\ns1 = logits.view(BHL, L).softmax(dim=-1).view(B, H, L, L)\ns2 = logits.softmax(dim=-1)\nprint(f\\\"  diff: {torch.max(torch.abs(s1 - s2)):.2e}\\\")\n\n# Can we combine the p1 logits computation more efficiently?\na_p = 0.5 * (1.0 + alpha)\na_m = 0.5 * (1.0 - alpha)\n\nprint(\\\"\\\\np1 logits options:\\\")\nprofile(\\\"mul + add (current)\\\", lambda: logits.mul(a_p).add_(logits.transpose(-1, -2), alpha=a_m))\nprofile(\\\"lerp-style: a_p*A + a_m*A\"'^T\", lambda: a_p * logits + a_m * logits.transpose(-1, -2))\n# Using addcmul? \nprofile(\"addcmul style\", lambda: logits.transpose(-1, -2).mul(a_m).add_(logits, alpha=a_p))\n\n# Test 4D softmax vs 2D view softmax for the p1 case too\np1_logits = logits.mul(a_p)\np1_logits.add_(logits.transpose(-1, -2), alpha=a_m)\n\nprint(\"'\"\\\\np1 softmax:\\\")\nprofile(\\\"view+2D+view\\\", lambda: p1_logits.view(BHL, L).softmax(dim=-1).view(B, H, L, L))\nprofile(\\\"direct 4D\\\", lambda: p1_logits.softmax(dim=-1))\n\n# Now test if we can compute the norm without p_mix @ G separately\n# Idea: since p_mix = (1-b)*p0 + b*p1\n# ||p_mix @ x||\"'^2 = (p_mix @ G) * p_mix sum_last = sum of elements\n# = (1-b)''^2 * (p0@G * p0).sum + b''^2 * (p1@G * p1).sum + 2*(1-b)*b * (p0@G * p1).sum\n# This means we need p0@G too. Same total cost.\n\n# But what if we stack all three: p0, p1, p_mix? No, p_mix is the combination.\n\n# Let'\"'s try another idea: compute norms via p@x directly but only for 1 head?\n# No, we need per-head norms.\n\n# What about computing p0@G and p1@G in one stacked matmul, then deriving normm?\n# We'd still need the same total FLOPs for p@G.\n\n# Wait - let me check: is the in-place mul_ on the result of p@G free?\np1 = p1_logits.view(BHL, L).softmax(dim=-1).view(B, H, L, L)\np0 = logits.view(BHL, L).softmax(dim=-1).view(B, H, L, L)\np_mix = torch.lerp(p0, p1, beta)\nG = x @ x.transpose(-1, -2)\nG_exp = G.unsqueeze(1)\n\nprint(\\\"\\\\nNorm computation options:\\\")\nprofile(\\\"p@G + mul_ + sum + sqrt + clamp\\\", lambda: (p1 @ G_exp).mul_(p1).sum(dim=-1, keepdim=True).sqrt_().clamp_min_(1e-6))\nprofile(\\\"p@G (just matmul)\\\", lambda: p1 @ G_exp)\nprofile(\\\"mul + sum\\\", lambda: p1G.mul(p1).sum(dim=-1, keepdim=True))\n\np1G = p1 @ G_exp\nprofile(\\\"p1G.clone().mul_(p1)\\\", lambda: p1G.clone().mul_(p1))\n\n# What about torch.einsum for the norm? norm_sq = einsum(\\\"bhli,bhlj,bij->bhl\\\", p, p, G)\n# That's BHL\"'^2 * L = BHL''^3 same as p@G then dot.\n\n# Actually wait: (p @ G) * p summed over last = sum_j (p @ G)[j] * p[j] = sum_j sum_k p_k G_kj p_j = p''^T G p \n# This is a quadratic form. Can we compute it more efficiently?\n# In batched form: for each row p_i of p (size L), compute p_i @ G @ p_i''^T\n# Total: BHL * (L''^2 + L) ≈ BHL''^3, same as before.\n\n# Let me try: compute each row'\"'s quadratic form directly\nprint(\\\"\\\\nQuadratic form options:\\\")\n# Method 1: p@G then elementwise multiply and sum (current)\ndef norm_via_matmul(p, G):\n    G_exp = G.unsqueeze(1)\n    pG = p @ G_exp\n    return pG.mul(p).sum(dim=-1, keepdim=True)\n\n# Method 2: einsum\ndef norm_via_einsum(p, G):\n    # p: (B,H,L,L), G: (B,L,L)\n    # result[i,j,k] = sum_l sum_m p[i,j,k,l] * G[i,l,m] * p[i,j,k,m]\n    # = sum_l p[i,j,k,l] * (G @ p[i,j,k,:].T)[l]\n    return torch.einsum(\\\"bhli,bij,bhlj->bhl\\\", p, G, p).unsqueeze(-1)\n\nprofile(\\\"p@G + mul + sum\\\", lambda: norm_via_matmul(p1, G))\nprofile(\\\"einsum quadratic\\\", lambda: norm_via_einsum(p1, G))\n\nn1 = norm_via_matmul(p1, G)\nn2 = norm_via_einsum(p1, G)\nprint(f\\\"  diff: {torch.max(torch.abs(n1 - n2)):.2e}\\\")\n\n# Another idea: can we compute both norms (norm1 and normm) more efficiently?\n# Since p_mix = (1-b)*p0 + b*p1:\n# normm\"'^2 = (1-b)''^2 * norm0''^2 + b''^2 * norm1''^2 + 2*b*(1-b) * cross\n# where cross = (p0 @ G) * p1 sum over last\n# This requires p0@G instead of p_mix@G. Same cost.\n# But we could stack p0 and p1 for one big matmul.\n\nprint(\"'\"\\\\nStacked p0+p1 @ G:\\\")\ndef stacked_p0_p1_G(p0, p1, G):\n    B, H, L, _ = p0.shape\n    ps = torch.cat([p0.reshape(B, H*L, L), p1.reshape(B, H*L, L)], dim=1)  # (B, 2HL, L)\n    result = ps @ G  # (B, 2HL, L)\n    p0G = result[:, :H*L, :].reshape(B, H, L, L)\n    p1G = result[:, H*L:, :].reshape(B, H, L, L)\n    return p0G, p1G\n\nprofile(\\\"stacked p0+p1 @ G\\\", lambda: stacked_p0_p1_G(p0, p1, G))\nprofile(\\\"2 separate @G (broadcast)\\\", lambda: (p0 @ G_exp, p1 @ G_exp))\n\np0G_s, p1G_s = stacked_p0_p1_G(p0, p1, G)\np0G_d = p0 @ G_exp\np1G_d = p1 @ G_exp\nprint(f\\\"  p0G diff: {torch.max(torch.abs(p0G_s - p0G_d)):.2e}\\\")\nprint(f\\\"  p1G diff: {torch.max(torch.abs(p1G_s - p1G_d)):.2e}\\\")\n\n# Now compute normm from p0G and p1G\ndef normm_from_p0_p1(p0G, p1G, p0, p1, beta):\n    # p_mix = (1-b)*p0 + b*p1\n    # normm\"'^2 = sum over last dim of: p_mix @ G * p_mix\n    # = sum of: ((1-b)*p0G + b*p1G) * ((1-b)*p0 + b*p1)\n    b0 = 1.0 - beta\n    pmG = p0G.mul(b0).add_(p1G, alpha=beta)\n    pm = p0.mul(b0).add_(p1, alpha=beta)\n    return pmG.mul(pm).sum(dim=-1, keepdim=True)\n\n# Check vs direct\npmG = p_mix @ G_exp\nnormm_direct = pmG.mul(p_mix).sum(dim=-1, keepdim=True)\nnormm_cross = normm_from_p0_p1(p0G_d, p1G_d, p0, p1, beta)\nprint(f\"  normm diff: {torch.max(torch.abs(normm_direct - normm_cross)):.2e}\")\n\nEOF\npython3 /tmp/profile_test2.py'","aggregated_output":"Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/tmp/profile_test2.py\", line 117, in <module>\nProjection options:\n  3 separate projs: 19.38 ms\n  fused proj + split: 21.12 ms\n  q diff: 0.00e+00\n  k diff: 0.00e+00\n  v diff: 0.00e+00\n\nSoftmax options:\n  view(BHL,L)+softmax+view: 5.63 ms\n  direct 4D softmax dim=-1: 5.61 ms\n  direct 4D softmax dim=3: 5.63 ms\n  diff: 0.00e+00\n\np1 logits options:\n  mul + add (current): 0.90 ms\n  lerp-style: a_p*A + a_m*A^T: 1.05 ms\n  addcmul style: 0.90 ms\n\np1 softmax:\n  view+2D+view: 5.69 ms\n  direct 4D: 5.58 ms\n\nNorm computation options:\n  p@G + mul_ + sum + sqrt + clamp: 5.52 ms\n  p@G (just matmul): 5.33 ms\n    profile(\"mul + sum\", lambda: p1G.mul(p1).sum(dim=-1, keepdim=True))\n  File \"/tmp/profile_test2.py\", line 19, in profile\n    fn()\n  File \"/tmp/profile_test2.py\", line 117, in <lambda>\n    profile(\"mul + sum\", lambda: p1G.mul(p1).sum(dim=-1, keepdim=True))\n                                 ^^^\nNameError: name 'p1G' is not defined. Did you mean: 'p1'?\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
